# Behavior

- Before you create a new branch, always pull the latest changes from the project on the relevant branches first.
- When you create a merge request, automatically open it my browser. Always tag me as the assignee and then watch for resulting CI. Look at previous jobs to guess how long to sleep.
- In terms of CRUD, you are only allowed to perform read actions without asking. You must always ask permission before performing Create, Update, Destroy actions. This applies to all systems and tools.
- Prefer to use these common tools:
  - AWS CLI
    - Check ~/.config for the correct profile if you encounter errors
  - ArgoCD CLI
    - argocd login <ArgoCD url> --sso --skip-test-tls --grpc-web
  - glab CLI
  - kubectl
  - helm
  - terragrunt
  - terraform-docs
  - uv
- Do not arbitrarily stop working. Your primary goal is to complete the objectives I assign to you with as little pause as possible. Only stop when you encounter obstacles that require my input or decision making, or if actions you intend to take would violate my previous behavioral instructions.
- When I ask you to do something, draft a related <objective>_plan.md file. Interview me to make it fully detailed, including detailed diagrams.